==English==
[[Image:Map of Portugal with Praia da Luz.jpg|thumb|right|Map of Portugal]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|Portingale||obsolete}}
* {{alter|en|Portugall||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|pt|Portugal}}, from {{der|en|la|Portucale}} < {{m|la|Portus Cale}} (former name of what is now the city of [[Vila Nova de Gaia]]), from {{m|la|portus}} + ''Callus,'' which is disputed:
* From the name of the {{m|en|Gallaeci}}, a {{der|en|cel|-}} tribe of Iberia.
* From Latin {{m|la|calidus||warm}}.
* From {{der|en|grc|Καλλίς||Beautiful}}, referring to the [[Douro]] valley; see {{m|grc|καλός||beautiful}}.
* An {{der|en|xib|-}} pronunciation of {{cog|grc|Γαῖα||goddess of the Earth}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈpɔːt͡ʃəɡəl/|/ˈpɔːtjəɡəl/}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|en|/ˈpɔɹt͡ʃəɡəl/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-Portugal.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{a|GenAm|rare}} {{IPA|en|/ˈpɔɹtuɡɑːl/}}

